chapter.v:
	(for Solomon 

	 had made a bronze platform five cubits long, five cubits wide, and three cubits high, and had set it in the midst of the court; and he stood on it, knelt down on his knees before all the assembly of Israel, and spread out his hands toward heaven);
 [1 Kin.]

	“When there 

	 is famine in the land, pestilence or blight or mildew, locusts or grasshoppers; when their enemies besiege them in the land of their cities; whatever plague or whatever sickness there is;
 [1 Kin. 10:28; 2 Chr. 1:16]

	then hear 

	 from heaven Your dwelling place, and forgive, and give to everyone according to all his ways, whose heart You know (for You alone know the hearts of the sons of men),
 [1 Kin. 4:21; 11:42, 43; 1 Chr.]
